#
# Counter-example for math:ConfidenceAsProbabilityConstraint (Rule P10): a
# math:ProbabilityValue that carries a logic:confidence (a confidence score read as its
# magnitude) but declares NO logic:probabilityModel to license the confidence→probability
# reading, so the SHACL-SPARQL constraint fires — shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent
# (math:ConfidenceAsProbability).
# Single violation: it carries a gmeow:hasReferenceFrame so the framing gate
# math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape (P3) stays SATISFIED (the sh:or hasReferenceFrame arm
# holds even though the probabilityModel arm is empty), it carries no math:quantityValue
# so the range gate math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape (P1) is vacuously satisfied, and it is
# not typed math:OddsValue / math:LogOddsValue so math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape (P2)
# stays satisfied — EXACTLY ONE finding, no sibling probability shape also fires.
# Back-reference: math:ProbabilityValue / math:ConfidenceAsProbability (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecConfidenceAsProbabilityBad).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:confidenceAsProbability a math:ProbabilityValue ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:extractionFrame ;
    logic:confidence "0.8"^^xsd:decimal .

ex:extractionFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .
<http://example.org/math/confidenceAsProbability> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
